{"symbol":"AKT3","resolved":{"input":"AKT3","symbol":"AKT3","ncbi_gene_id":"10000","name":"AKT serine/threonine kinase 3","location":"1q43-q44","aliases":["MPPH","MPPH2","PKB-GAMMA","PKBG","PRKBG","RAC-PK-gamma","RAC-gamma","STK-2"],"uniprot":"Q9Y243","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"AKT3 function (UniProt Q9Y243, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): AKT3 is one of 3 closely related serine/threonine-protein kinases (AKT1, AKT2 and AKT3) called the AKT kinase, and which regulate many processes including metabolism, proliferation, cell survival, growth and angiogenesis. This is mediated through serine and/or threonine phosphorylation of a range of downstream substrates. Over 100 substrate candidates have been reported so far, but for most of them, no isoform specificity has been reported. AKT3 is the least studied AKT isoform. It plays an important role in brain development and is crucial for the viability of malignant glioma cells. AKT3 isoform may also be the key molecule in up-regulation and down-regulation of MMP13 via IL13. Required ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q9Y243","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q9Y243/entry","title":"AKT3: RAC-gamma serine/threonine-protein kinase"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:18524868","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18524868/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:21191416","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21191416/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"AKT3 GO biological process annotations: negative regulation of cellular senescence, positive regulation of blood vessel endothelial cell migration, positive regulation of cell migration involved in sprouting angiogenesis, positive regulation of endothelial cell proliferation, positive regulation of vascular endothelial cell proliferation, regulation of mitochondrion organization, signal transduction","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q9Y243","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q9Y243/entry","title":"AKT3: RAC-gamma serine/threonine-protein kinase"}]},{"text":"AKT3 GO biological process annotations: insulin receptor signaling pathway, intracellular signal transduction, negative regulation of apoptotic process, negative regulation of PERK-mediated unfolded protein response, positive regulation of angiogenesis, positive regulation of artery morphogenesis","evidence":"computationally predicted","code":"PRED","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q9Y243","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q9Y243/entry","title":"AKT3: RAC-gamma serine/threonine-protein kinase"}]}],"pathways":[{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-111447","name":"Activation of BAD and translocation to mitochondria ","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-111447","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-1257604","name":"PIP3 activates AKT signaling","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-1257604","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-1358803","name":"Downregulation of ERBB2:ERBB3 signaling","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-1358803","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-165159","name":"MTOR signalling","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-165159","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-165181","name":"Inhibition of TSC complex formation by AKT (PKB)","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-165181","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-198323","name":"AKT phosphorylates targets in the cytosol","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-198323","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"AKT3","id":"R-HSA-198693","name":"AKT phosphorylates targets in the nucleus","url":"https://reactome.org/content/d